# QM/MM on a real peptide (2E4E, a de novo designed GPM12 mutant, 129 atoms,
# AMBER-14): one step of ground-state QM/MM dynamics, i.e. the embedded QM/MM
# energy and forces at the input geometry.
# QM = GLY1 plus the TYR2 backbone N/CA, so the partition cuts the TYR2 CA-CB
# bond; the cut is capped with a hydrogen link atom and the default
# frontier_scheme=none (full-field ESPF) is used.  The N-terminal NH3+ gives
# the QM region charge +1.  Requires OpenMM.
#
# This used to be a runtype=energy deck.  The plain single-point route never
# builds the ESPF embedding records (OQP::ESPF_CORR / OQP::POTQM) -- only the
# force-based QM/MM driver behind md(...), optimize(...) and namd(...) does --
# so it aborted inside the SCF.  One md step is the supported spelling.
rks/bhhlyp/6-31g* charge=1 md(nstep=1,dt=0.5,velocity=zero,ensemble=nve) dftgrid(rad_type=becke)
qmmm(forcefield_files="amber14-all.xml",qm_atoms="0-10,21,22",cutoff=NoCutoff)
geom="2E4E.pdb"
